Returning, Remembrance, Presence, Protection from lower movements,
Raise the Consciousness, Peace, Hastening, Strength, Refind will to Shield / Offer,
Spiritual Romance, Asking, Acknowledge Grace

### **4.2.4 - Pray For**

Pray for knowledge and light, every other prayer is selfish. ~ Swami Vivekananda, C.W. I. 146

Our constant prayer is to understand the Divine's will and to live accordingly. ~ The Mother, Words Of The Mother II, Elements of Yoga, Surrender to the Divine Will, Surrender

Aspiration is a turning upward of the inner being with a call, yearning, prayer for the Divine, for the Truth, for the Consciousness, Peace, Ananda, Knowledge, descent of Divine Force or whatever else is the aim of one's endeavour. ~ The Mother, [T2], #index,

If the only prayer you said was thank you, that would be enough. ~ Meister Eckhart

Pray without ceasing for light and love and self-surrender to the Divine Mother - these are the elements of Bhakti. ~ Sri Ramakrishna

We pray to God for Bliss and receive it by Grace. The bestower of bliss must be Bliss itself and also Infinite. ~ Sri Ramana Maharshi

When waking up every morning, let us pray for a day of complete consecration. With my blessings ~ The Mother, Mantras Of The Mother, 19 June,

### **4.2.5 - How to Pray**

No prayer is complete without prescence ~ Jalaluddin Rumi,

The whole of our life should be a prayer offered to the Divine. ~ The Mother, Words Of The Mother III,

All sincere prayers are granted, but it may take some time to realise materially. ~ The Mother, Words Of The Mother III,

When naked of ego and mind it hears the Voice  ~ Sri Aurobindo, Savitri, The Kingdoms and Godheads of the Greater Mind, [T5],

Prayer begins at the edge of emptiness. ~ Rabbi Abraham Joshua Heschel,

Do not reduce your prayers to words, but rather make the totality of your life a prayer to God. ~ Isaac of Nineveh,

Fortune resists half-hearted prayers. ~ Ovid,

Pray without ceasing. ~ Anonymous, The Bible, Thessalonians, 1, 5:17,

He who labours, prays. ~ Saint Augustine of Hippo,

Prayers should be full of confidence without sorrow or lamenting. ~ Sri Aurobindo,

The Supreme's power is infinite -it is our faith that is small. With my Blessings. ~ The Mother, Mantras Of The Mother, 23 August

Pray to Him anyway you like, He can even hear the footfall of an ant. ~ Sri Ramakrishna

When the mind and speech unite in earnest, asking for a thing, that prayer is answered. ~ Sri Ramakrishna,

All sincere prayers are granted, every call is answered. With my blessings, ~ The Mother, Mantras Of The Mother,

In centering prayer, the sacred word is not the object of the attention but rather the expression of the intention of the will. ~ Thomas Keating,

In prayer, more is accomplished by listening than by talking. Let us leave to God the decisions as to what shall be said. ~ Saint Francis de Sales

Humility is necessary for the person praying, because he recognizes his neediness ~ Saint Thomas Aquinas, (ST 2-2.83.15).

The prayer of faith is the only kind that is real prayer, and it is trust in God with full acknowledgment of God's power and love. ~ Archibald Thomas Robertson

He who fights even the smallest distractions faithfully, when he says even the smallest prayer, will also be faithful in great things. ~ Saint Louis de Montfort

A real prayer will never contain any suggestions, instructions or demands. In real prayer you bow down, surrender and declare your helplessness to the Lord. ~ MATA AMRITANANDAMAYI,

### **4.2.6 - PRAYER ATTEMPTS**

1. O LORD, I implore Thee, grant me Thy Strength that I may be faithful to the Master, that I may resist all non-soul movements, that I do not tarry backwards, nor in circles, but rather that each moment is a conscious step towards Thee.
2. O LORD, I implore Thee, may I at least, take one more step towards Thee, then, Master, may there me at least one additional offering to the soul, in Thy Hastening.

### **4.2.7 - Prayer Statements**

LORD, grant me Thy strenth,
to abstain, resist, reject and refuse, for the sacred No,
to shoulder my duty with gratitude,
to walk without ceasing to Thee and thy Will,
that I am faithful to my faith,
that I resist backward movements,

